WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.960
NICK: Niko is about to...

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:03.600
Do something FRICKIN' CRAZY.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.040
He's about to DROP A TAPE in DIRT

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:09.100
NIKO: One tape please.

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:10.140
NICK: One tape!

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.560
NIKO: I've heard that LiPo batteries are really dangerous.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:14.520
So we have this really puffed up LiPo battery,

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.400
and it's a really old battery, it's been used a million times...

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.240
WREN: A million times...

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.400
NIKO: ...Slight exaggeration.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.080
Anyway, you're not supposed to use them when they get puffy.

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:22.300
I figured, let's see what happens

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.300
if I pierce it through the heart with an arrow

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.360
NICK: Where is the heart of a battery located?

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.120
NIKO: Uhh, right in the smack-dab center.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:30.200
The battery's like the heart of your electronics...

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.780
...Uh, yeah, I dunno what it actually is.
NICK: [laughter]

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:34.260
Carmichael, what do you think's gonna happen?

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:38.720
Nick, what do you think's gonna happen?

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:40.180
NICK: I think it's gonna fuckin' explode.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:41.200
NIKO: [laughter]

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.080
CARMICHAEL: Wren, you're an engineer, will it explode?

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.520
NIKO: Oh! Just fell off the tape.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.020
CARMICHAEL: 'Cause you watered the board!

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:52.280
NIKO: So it wouldn't light on fire!

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:53.840
It's not fallin' down this time.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:56.820
I'm hoping this is a little bit of a show.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:59.680
I'm hoping that we haven't enticed you with an exploding battery...

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.120
...just to have it sit there.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:07.260
[Arrow impacts]

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:08.320
NIKO: Too high.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:12.140
[Arrow impacts]

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:14.180
Niko: All right, need to pull it out again.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:17.320
[Arrow impacts]
NIKO: [quietly] Aww!

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:19.240
[Arrow impacts]

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:28.360
[Flames hissing]

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:30.560
ALL: Whoa!

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:32.480
CARMICHAEL: Whoa!

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:33.580
NIKO: Holy crap!

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:37.940
NIKO: Whoo, baby!

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:42.480
NIKO: [laughter]

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:44.160
NIKO: That... was great!

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.040
WREN: Oh, god!
CARMICHAEL: Whoa!

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:50.880
WREN: Oh god, oh god!
CARMICHAEL: Round Two, Round Two!

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:53.480
NICK: Holy shit!

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.180
NICK and NIKO: [laughter]

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:56.120
NIKO: The arrow is done...

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.900
NICK: Hold on, hold on, hold on, hold on.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:00.260
CARMICHAEL: Oh, film it in slow--

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:03.500
ALL: [exclaiming and laughing]

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:04.820
ALL: Whoa!

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:15.140
WREN: That totally makes sense, 'cause isn't that a three-cell battery?
NIKO: Yeah.

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:16.920
WREN: Three... Three burnings!

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:20.960
That FAR surpassed my expectations! Holy crap! That was amazing!

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:22.360
NIKO: Yeah, we didn't want Wren to, like...

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:23.920
...We wanted Wren to hype it up in the beginning,

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:26.140
to make it like -- the video seem all exciting, but he wouldn't do it,

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:26.740
'cause he's all like,

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:29.560
[imitating Wren] "Tsk, I'm an engineering student, and batteries don't explode."

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:31.520
WREN: No-- I-- That was not the case!
NIKO: [laughter]

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:34.280
NIKO: Turns out, Wren's expectations... were surpassed!

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:35.740
NICK: Dude, look at the arrow!

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:39.380
NIKO: The thing is, when you charge it, all that electricity releases all at once!

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:44.600
CARMICHAEL: Oh, there's still an arrow in there!

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:47.980
NIKO: If I don't wear this hat, people won't know which channel I'm with!

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.260
NIKO: Turns out they weren't lying about LiPo batteries.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:53.660
Look at that.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:55.500
SAM: Did it straight up explode?

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:59.720
NIKO: Hah, close. It, uh, it just shot out a jet of flame, like, this long.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:03.720
SAM: Oh, that's cool. I wish I could've known you guys had been doing that. That'd be fun to watch.

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:05.240
NIKO: I guess you can watch the replay.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:11.860
SAM: One take! First try!

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:13.060
First try!

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:13.860
I can do this...

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:18.100
ALL: [exclaiming]

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:19.560
SAM: Yeah, like that.

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:21.740
ALL: [exclaiming]
NICK: Oh, one take, first try!

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:24.400
SAM: One take, first try!

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:26.480
ALL: [exclaiming]

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:27.840
NIKO: First try.
SAM: First try, first try.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:31.160
WREN: Oh! [laughter]

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:33.000
D: Wow, that was one take, that's crazy.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.480
SAM: I can't believe you did it-- like, you made it perfectly in the first take on the first try.

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:38.180
NIKO: One take, first try, all the way back here!

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:39.380
D: Yup! Here we go!

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:44.200
ALL: [exclaiming]

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:49.200
NIKO: Ladies and gentlemen, this is the last day to get your very own Corridor Digital hat.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.320
The reason we do them limited edition is because we actually have to make them to order,

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:55.240
so we take the number of people that ordered them and make that many hats.

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:57.160
So if you want one, today is the day.

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:59.860
I'm personally a big fan of the new yellow and black colors.

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:03.440
CARMICHAEL: There's on average about four to five people working in this studio.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:06.000
Nick and I can't always be there to film them.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:09.020
We have a great workshop designed for the builders,

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:10.380
not the cameramen.

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:12.420
Simply put, we need a top-down rig.

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:16.140
I'm going to build the best-moving top-down rig for this workshop.

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:18.320
SPENCER: Top-down rig's only $224.

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:20.900
CARMICHAEL: Minus the camera.
SPENCER: Minus the camera and the light.

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:23.900
CARMICHAEL: Here's the plan for the top-down rig that Spencer and I designed.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.920
First we're gonna mount brackets onto the walls.

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:29.000
Then we string up two sets of wires across the room,

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.720
horizontally on both sides.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:33.740
That provides us lateral movement from left to right.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:37.000
The next step is to cut two boards that go on those cables,

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.160
with one board on each side of the room

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:42.000
We attach them with four cables and four tensioners.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.520
These board have four pulley wheels on the back of them

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:46.740
so they can slide left to right on the cables.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:51.500
Next step is to cut and build the camera dolly that goes in the center of these four cables,

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:55.960
which allows us to go bilaterally across the room in a way that we couldn't before.

00:04:57.080 --> 00:05:02.160
CARMICHAEL: Spencer has built the entire top-down rig as a 3D model in 3ds Max.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:06.620
Functional - so we can have a better idea of physically what's going to be, virtually.

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:21.640
SPENCER: So here's the very unfun part.

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:25.360
I'm curious - There probably is a tool to do this, but I don't own it.

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:27.760
CARMICHAEL: So you're just hand-screwing it for now?
SPENCER: I have to.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.000
Stick thing in, and rotate thing.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:42.660
SAM: One take, first try!

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:44.220
[laughter]

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:46.480
SAM: One take, first try!

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:48.980
D: First try.

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:50.520
[laughter]
D: Hold on-

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:54.180
D: One try.
[laughter]

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:55.880
D: God dang it.

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:58.680
NIKO: Wren, you want something cool?

00:05:58.680 --> 00:05:59.860
WREN: What's that?

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:02.900
NIKO: We did this mixed reality video for Node.

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:04.600
We've been doing it for a couple of weeks now.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:06.140
[Wren crashes]

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:08.900
NIKO: Holy moly, you okay?
WREN: Yeah.

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:11.460
NIKO: The video that just came out today - looks crazy.
WREN: Yeah?

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:14.340
NIKO: Yeah, like as a video effects guy, I think you'll really appreciate it.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:17.160
We figured out a way where we take a third controller that's tracked in 3D space

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:20.080
and you put it on the camera, and that gives you a virtual camera

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:22.820
that's doing the same thing your real-life camera is doing.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:24.900
So you take the footage from the virtual camera,

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:26.540
and you combine it with footage from the real camera.

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:29.560
It looks like the stuff you're filming is in real life as long as it's on a green screen.

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:31.400
It looks like it's in that virtual space.

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:33.380
There's this game called Gorn, which is a fighting game.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:35.680
It works flawlessly with mixed reality.

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:37.660
WREN: Oh man.
NIKO: Like, it has perfect foreground layers.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:39.760
WREN: Dude, the key to this is having those foreground layers.
NIKO: Yeah.

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:42.020
NIKO: It keeps track of where the headset is in space,

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:45.220
and any models between the headset and the camera - it renders out as a separate layer.

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:49.040
The part where Sam grabs two arms and just starts like poundin' the ground with them...

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:52.600
WREN: [exclaims, laughter]
NIKO: Look at this. Look how crazy that looks!

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:56.780
The tracking, the foreground layers, the compositing - like, it all works out so well.

00:06:56.780 --> 00:07:00.420
Like, I'm in that space, just making blood triangles fly everywhere.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:03.160
WREN: We should do, like, an entire short film based on this.

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:04.400
NIKO: Yeah, I'm kinda thinking we should, too.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:07.060
The visual effects side of me is like, I'm really excited about this.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:10.740
I really wanna make a GIF of this, 'cause I think this'll hit  the front page of Reddit.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.720
I'll do it right when this vlog is posted,

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:14.880
and I'll put a link in the comments so you guys can go upvote it

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:16.140
and we can hit the front page of Reddit.

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:17.960
Would you guys like a GIF making tutorial?

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:19.920
If you would, let us know in the comments below

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:22.420
and we'll put one in one of our upcoming vlogs,

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:24.840
and maybe we can actually do like a little GIF film festival,

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:28.440
where everybody makes GIFs of, I dunno, their favorite parts from a Sam and Niko video,

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:29.360
or something like that.

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:31.360
There's only like, a billion Corridor Digital GIFs out there

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:33.380
but Sam and Niko channel needs a little bit of love.

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:34.740
If you guys wanna check out the full video, it's on Node

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:37.960
so head on over there to watch us live in a virtual realm.

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:40.640
WREN: Isn't all the Big Bear weekend stuff going up soon?

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:44.420
with all the Nerf gang?
NIKO: Yeah, every Wednesday now, going forward.

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:47.620
SAM: Every Wednesday for the next two months.
NICK: Holy moly.

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:48.740
[Nick speaking]

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:52.220
[laughter]

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:54.600
CARMICHAEL: What's the fit?

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:56.260
SPENCER: Fits in goooood, lookin' good!

00:07:57.160 --> 00:08:00.360
SPENCER: We're ready to string our first layer!

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:04.280
And then we need to cut some wood - the first set of wheels on,

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:07.360
tension some more, and we'll be golden!

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:09.540
SPENCER: Time to swedge.

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:12.120
What it does is that we have this little piece of aluminum here,

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:15.340
and a swedger closes that aluminum down on it,

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:17.500
so it doesn't... move.

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:22.780
SPENCER:  Without really, actually tightening the middle-

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:25.580
Increase the tension of the walls -

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:27.560
you're the ex-engineer,

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:31.080
Is that more of an exponential pull, or is it more of a -

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:32.480
WREN: Like a linear pull?
SPENCER: Yeah, linear.

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:33.760
WREN: Linear increase?

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:37.140
WREN: The crux of the issue is that you need to be able to make this really really tight

00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:40.620
so that this doesn't sag. The issue is that when you do that, you're pulling this away

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:44.200
putting a lot of extra tension on these wires which are attached to the walls.

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:48.180
SPENCER: I really wanna know how many pounds we're pulling on the wall there

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:50.680
There's only so much a 2x4 can hold.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:51.840
WREN: [sighs]

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:56.300
Here, it's a matter of how strong is the connection of the 2x4 to the roof

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:59.740
for whatever studs that the 2x4 studs are connected to.

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:02.420
SPENCER: I'm more worried about here, 'cause this is a pressure point

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:04.620
where the threads are digging into the wood

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:08.500
WREN: So you're saying - you think that this screw point itself might fail.

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:11.920
SPENCER: Oh I think - I think that screw point will fail before anything else, for sure.

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:15.460
SPENCER: Our plan of attack, as I said, is:

00:09:15.460 --> 00:09:19.380
we leave the top ones on, replace one wire at a time

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:22.860
making this as tight as we can with, like, unscrewing these.

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:28.160
WREN: I'd say, yeah, just one at a time, pull these cables until the whole system's tight.

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:31.600
SPENCER: From a technical standpoint, this should be easier

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:34.980
than dealing with poles and finding the hardware, and cheaper.

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:39.600
WREN: I feel like going the pole route would've been easier... to be honest.

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:48.220
CARMICHAEL: I just wanna go home.

00:09:50.180 --> 00:09:54.060
NIKO: Get that shield outta my face. Get that shield outta my face!

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:59.880
[exclaiming, game sound effects]

